# TypeScript Standards

- Strict mode is enabled. Do not use `// @ts-ignore` or `any` without justification.
- Define interfaces for component props. Use `type` for unions/aliases, `interface` for object shapes.
- All shared types live in `src/shared/types/index.ts`.
- Prefer explicit return types on exported functions.
- Handle errors with try/catch and `console.error`, never silently swallow errors.
